### MojoPay integration — manual request book
### Fill in the variables below, then run requests with the VS Code REST Client extension.

@paymentApiUrl = https://portal.cs-pay.app
@invoiceApiUrl = https://api.cs-pay.app/v1
@collectionBaseUrl = https://api.cs-pay.app/v3
@directDebitBaseUrl = https://api-dev.cs-pay.app/v3/dd

@appId = 3979971769
@apiKey = 46265147
# base64("{{appId}}:{{apiKey}}") — regenerate if either credential changes
@collectionAuth = Basic Mzk3OTk3MTc2OTo0NjI2NTE0Nw==
@ddAppId = your-dd-app-id
@ddAppKey = your-dd-app-key

@mobile = +233543460633
@network = MTN
@feeTypeCode = your-fee-type-code
@orderId = TEST-ORDER-0001
@mandateId = replace-after-mandate-approved
@merchantReferenceId = TEST-MANDATE-0001


### ============================================================
### Hosted checkout (MojoPayIntegration)
### ============================================================

### Initiate payment — returns redirect_url for the hosted page
# @name initiatePayment
POST {{paymentApiUrl}}/interapi/ProcessPayment
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "app_id": "{{appId}}",
  "app_key": "{{apiKey}}",
  "name": "Test Donor",
  "mobile": "{{mobile}}",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "feetypecode": "{{feeTypeCode}}",
  "currency": "GHS",
  "amount": 1,
  "order_id": "{{orderId}}",
  "order_desc": "Test donation",
  "return_url": "https://example.com/payment/callback"
}

### Query invoice status — status_message "PAID BY CLIENT" means completed
POST {{invoiceApiUrl}}/Interapi.svc/QueryInvoiceStatus
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "app_id": "{{appId}}",
  "app_key": "{{apiKey}}",
  "order_id": "{{orderId}}"
}


### ============================================================
### Collection / direct momo charge (MojoCollectionIntegration)
### Basic auth: base64(appId:apiKey)
### ============================================================

### Init payment — pushes a prompt to the customer's phone
# @name collectionInitPayment
POST {{collectionBaseUrl}}/api/payments/initpayment
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{collectionAuth}}

{
  "CustomerName": "Test Donor",
  "Network": "{{network}}",
  "Mobile": "{{mobile}}",
  "Email": "test@example.com",
  "Currency": "GHS",
  "CountryCode": "GHA",
  "Amount": 1,
  "OrderId": "{{orderId}}",
  "OrderDesc": "Test donation"
}

### Query collection status
GET {{collectionBaseUrl}}/api/payments/status/{{orderId}}
Authorization: {{collectionAuth}}


### ============================================================
### Direct debit (MojoDirectDebitIntegration)
### Run ddAuth first — every other DD request reuses its AccessToken.
### ============================================================

### Authenticate
# @name ddAuth
POST {{directDebitBaseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "AppId": "{{ddAppId}}",
  "AppKey": "{{ddAppKey}}"
}

### Create mandate — customer approves the prompt on their phone
POST {{directDebitBaseUrl}}/api/mandate/create-mandate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ddAuth.response.body.AccessToken}}

{
  "Mobile": "{{mobile}}",
  "Network": "{{network}}",
  "Amount": 1,
  "Currency": "GHS",
  "Frequency": "MONTHLY",
  "FeeType": "DIRECTDEBIT",
  "Country": "GHA",
  "StartDate": "2026-08-01",
  "EndDate": "2027-08-01",
  "DayOfDebit": 1,
  "PlatformScheduling": true,
  "Data": {
    "MerchantReferenceId": "{{merchantReferenceId}}",
    "Description": "Monthly recurring donation"
  }
}

### Mandate status — 404 with StatusCode DD_NOT_FOUND when unknown
GET {{directDebitBaseUrl}}/api/mandate/status?MerchantReferenceId={{merchantReferenceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ddAuth.response.body.AccessToken}}

### Cancel mandate
POST {{directDebitBaseUrl}}/api/mandate/cancel-mandate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ddAuth.response.body.AccessToken}}

{
  "Mobile": "{{mobile}}",
  "MandateId": "{{mandateId}}",
  "Reason": "Customer requested cancellation"
}

### Direct debit payment status
POST {{directDebitBaseUrl}}/api/DirectDebit/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ddAuth.response.body.AccessToken}}

{
  "MandateId": "{{mandateId}}",
  "TransactionReferenceId": "{{orderId}}"
}